      "writtenOn": "2023-04-07T19:33:36Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "One of the reasons for having RenderSteps declaring the Uniforms in C++ was so that the declarations could be automatically generated.\n\nDo you think in a follow-up that that would be a reasonable direction to go towards? Or does the fact that it returns a complete SkSL program (or an externally defined program) make that not a very important convenience to have?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 524,
        "startChar": 50,
        "endLine": 524,
        "endChar": 78
      },
      "revId": "218b2fcd55134f76e5c35ff17bea4c807da6b238",
      "serverId": "5086850b-e599-37d2-8ec8-ff16aeccbf02"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "6c9f8a9e_a405c07d",
        "filename": "tests/graphite/ComputeTest.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 7
      },
      "lineNbr": 524,
      "author": {
        "id": 18529
      },
      "writtenOn": "2023-04-27T20:49:20Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "With the current model in which ComputeSteps only declare resources and already have to implement logic to encode storage and uniforms buffers dynamically, I didn\u0027t feel that having a special convenience for uniforms added much value.\n\nThe fact that a ComputeStep defines a complete program without a prescribed design for how UBO/SSBO data gets laid out is one big difference compared to RenderSteps (which is why I didn\u0027t define this in terms of a PipelineDataGatherer).\n\nThis might potentially change as this gets revised for batched draw processing for geometry steps. In that model, we may want per-draw uniform data that get laid out and indexed similarly to RenderStep uniforms. I think for geometry processing steps it makes sense to have a prescribed model for data bindings that perhaps works at a higher-level than a ComputeStep. Perhaps having a GeometryStep specialization of ComputeStep could define methods that are more batching oriented and layered on top of the data flow smarts provided by ComputeStep/DispatchGroup.\n\nThis is worth a revisit as I re-focus on geometry steps once the Vello-based AA work has settled.\n\nI filed b/279955342 and documented my current thoughts around this issue.",
      "parentUuid": "97a16731_5d8ee35d",
